            <ArticleTitle>Impact of hypertension, overall obesity and abdominal obesity on diabetes incidence in Shanghai residents with different glucose levels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e59-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2011.08.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The impact of hypertension, overall obesity and abdominal obesity, individually or collectively, on diabetes incidence over a period of 5 years in residents with different glucose levels is diverse, with abdominal obesity having an impact in both non-diabetic hyperglycaemia and normal groups.</AbstractText>
